1
00:00:05,083 --> 00:00:06,375
Ahh...

2
00:00:06,375 --> 00:00:11,916
the final two Prismatic Blades
are in the hands of my servants.

3
00:00:13,583 --> 00:00:15,166
False dragons!

4
00:00:15,166 --> 00:00:17,583
You seven cosmic frauds!

5
00:00:17,583 --> 00:00:20,250
You've kept me
from what I deserve for eons,

6
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:24,541
but soon... I will rise!

7
00:00:26,625 --> 00:00:29,791
It's true. My parents are dead.

8
00:00:29,791 --> 00:00:32,041
I saw the headstones myself.

9
00:00:32,041 --> 00:00:34,208
I didn't even get
to say goodbye to them.

10
00:00:34,208 --> 00:00:37,500
[wind blowing]

11
00:00:39,458 --> 00:00:41,375
Aw, man.

12
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:44,625
Arin, I'm so sorry.

13
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:48,916
How did...?

14
00:00:48,916 --> 00:00:51,875
I mean, what happened?

15
00:00:51,875 --> 00:00:53,625
The Merge happened!

16
00:00:53,625 --> 00:00:56,500
My parents died
because of what Master Wu did!

17
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:59,083
If my uncle
really caused the Merge,

18
00:00:59,083 --> 00:01:01,250
I have to believe
he had a good reason.

19
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:04,666
No reason makes it okay
that my family died!

20
00:01:04,666 --> 00:01:08,208
No, I didn't mean... I just...

21
00:01:08,208 --> 00:01:09,916
But more people will die

22
00:01:09,916 --> 00:01:12,833
if the Forbidden Five
use those blades,

23
00:01:12,833 --> 00:01:14,750
and I need Ras back.

24
00:01:14,750 --> 00:01:17,000
So you want to work with us?

25
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
If... if that's okay.

26
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Of course it is.

27
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,458
You're one of us.

28
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:24,958
I concur.

29
00:01:24,958 --> 00:01:27,291
Was hoping we'd get
to fight together.

30
00:01:27,291 --> 00:01:29,708
I'd rather risk my life
with my best friend

31
00:01:29,708 --> 00:01:32,125
than be safe without you.

32
00:01:33,666 --> 00:01:36,041
Then let's get going.

33
00:01:36,041 --> 00:01:38,125
Not to precipitate
on this procession,

34
00:01:38,125 --> 00:01:39,916
but given the rate
Drix was traveling

35
00:01:39,916 --> 00:01:42,041
with the final two
Prismatic Blades,

36
00:01:42,041 --> 00:01:44,583
catching up to him
before he reaches ThunderFang

37
00:01:44,583 --> 00:01:46,166
is an impossibility.

38
00:01:46,166 --> 00:01:48,958
Impossible as in...
it can't happen?

39
00:01:48,958 --> 00:01:51,833
Yes, I am indeed using
the word "impossible"

40
00:01:51,833 --> 00:01:53,125
to mean "impossible."

41
00:01:53,125 --> 00:01:54,791
I hate Drix.

42
00:01:54,791 --> 00:01:57,666
Second worst time I've had
fighting insects.

43
00:01:57,666 --> 00:01:59,750
First time was
that picnic with Jay.

44
00:01:59,750 --> 00:02:01,958
That was my picnic with Jay.

45
00:02:01,958 --> 00:02:03,083
I didn't invite you!

46
00:02:03,083 --> 00:02:05,458
And I told you not
to rub honey in your hair!

47
00:02:05,458 --> 00:02:07,708
Well, Jay double-dog dared me!

48
00:02:07,708 --> 00:02:09,833
I didn't want to back out
and look uncool.

49
00:02:09,833 --> 00:02:11,125
[Sora] Did you miss this?

50
00:02:11,125 --> 00:02:12,458
"Look uncool"? [laughing]

51
00:02:12,458 --> 00:02:14,333
Did running
through the Monastery

52
00:02:14,333 --> 00:02:17,791
with a swarm of clamp-beetles
on your tail look cool?

53
00:02:17,791 --> 00:02:19,583
Yes, I happen to think that--

54
00:02:19,583 --> 00:02:20,500
[Lloyd] Hold it.

55
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:22,583
"Through the Monastery."

56
00:02:22,583 --> 00:02:23,916
That's it.

57
00:02:23,916 --> 00:02:26,041
I know how to beat Drix.

58
00:02:26,041 --> 00:02:28,666
[wind howling]

59
00:02:28,666 --> 00:02:31,958
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

60
00:02:31,958 --> 00:02:34,833
♪ Together we will rise ♪

61
00:02:34,833 --> 00:02:38,333
♪ We fight ♪

62
00:02:38,333 --> 00:02:41,416
♪ Be a ninja
for what's right ♪

63
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:43,625
[thunderclap]

64
00:02:43,625 --> 00:02:45,208
[♪♪♪]

65
00:02:45,791 --> 00:02:47,416
[Wyldfyre] What do you mean,

66
00:02:47,416 --> 00:02:49,375
"He won't
survive much longer"?

67
00:02:49,375 --> 00:02:50,833
Is that med-bot talk

68
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:52,666
for "He's definitely
getting better"?

69
00:02:52,666 --> 00:02:54,000
It is not.

70
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,625
It is only a matter of time

71
00:02:55,625 --> 00:02:57,916
before Roby's
vital signs will cease.

72
00:02:57,916 --> 00:03:00,375
The same for the dragon.

73
00:03:00,375 --> 00:03:02,166
Wrong answer.

74
00:03:02,166 --> 00:03:03,958
There has to be
something we can do.

75
00:03:03,958 --> 00:03:06,291
Check all those
boring books again.

76
00:03:06,291 --> 00:03:08,500
We have searched every volume
in the library

77
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:10,250
several times for any--

78
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:11,666
Check them again!

79
00:03:16,250 --> 00:03:18,041
Read this. Read that.

80
00:03:18,041 --> 00:03:19,416
Already read it.
Waste of my time.

81
00:03:19,416 --> 00:03:20,958
-[dragon shrieking]
-What--?

82
00:03:22,708 --> 00:03:25,416
You're worried about
your friend too, huh?

83
00:03:30,708 --> 00:03:33,083
Hey! Don't do that!

84
00:03:38,041 --> 00:03:39,416
[squawking]

85
00:04:07,458 --> 00:04:09,500
And... done.

86
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:10,500
[grumbling contentedly]

87
00:04:13,833 --> 00:04:15,541
Personal reward time!

88
00:04:19,208 --> 00:04:22,250
Mm, candied zip-flies!

89
00:04:24,416 --> 00:04:26,125
Whoa! Wha-wha whoa...

90
00:04:40,250 --> 00:04:41,500
[skidding]

91
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:43,000
[Mr. Frohicky] Careful!
I just waxed the--

92
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,041
Oh, my mirror finish!

93
00:04:45,041 --> 00:04:46,916
This is a shoes-off temple!

94
00:04:49,666 --> 00:04:51,500
Aah!

95
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:56,333
Tragically, my polishing skills
are unparalleled.

96
00:04:56,333 --> 00:04:58,791
My<i> apolish</i>-gies.

97
00:04:58,791 --> 00:05:00,791
[chortling]

98
00:05:00,791 --> 00:05:02,000
Master Zane, did you get that?

99
00:05:03,791 --> 00:05:04,666
Wha-ha-ha!

100
00:05:05,916 --> 00:05:10,625
Zane, how long
will Lloyd's plan take?

101
00:05:10,625 --> 00:05:12,375
Set-up should only take
a few minutes,

102
00:05:12,375 --> 00:05:14,333
if all goes as intended.

103
00:05:14,333 --> 00:05:16,250
We have only done this
once before,

104
00:05:16,250 --> 00:05:18,875
and it was not intentionally
planned that time.

105
00:05:18,875 --> 00:05:21,416
A few minutes is all I need.

106
00:05:21,416 --> 00:05:22,625
Whaa!

107
00:05:22,625 --> 00:05:23,500
[Nya] For what?

108
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:24,666
To build you all something

109
00:05:24,666 --> 00:05:27,708
to even the odds against Drix
and the Dragonians.

110
00:05:27,708 --> 00:05:28,791
Whoa!

111
00:05:28,791 --> 00:05:30,583
You all heard Zane.
We only have a few minutes

112
00:05:30,583 --> 00:05:33,083
to grab supplies, weapons,
anything you need.

113
00:05:33,083 --> 00:05:35,458
Meet back
in the Dragon Stables!

114
00:05:35,458 --> 00:05:37,916
[all slipping]

115
00:05:37,916 --> 00:05:38,791
[sighing]

116
00:05:38,791 --> 00:05:40,666
Well, I wasn't really interested

117
00:05:40,666 --> 00:05:43,500
in personal rewards anyway.

118
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:45,125
Back to work.

119
00:05:45,125 --> 00:05:46,000
Aah! Ow.

120
00:05:53,416 --> 00:05:57,041
[wistful music playing]

121
00:06:01,916 --> 00:06:04,416
[peaceful music playing]

122
00:06:06,416 --> 00:06:07,916
[laughing]

123
00:06:11,166 --> 00:06:12,208
[munching]

124
00:06:15,583 --> 00:06:17,125
[munching]

125
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,958
Sorry, just came
to grab some parts.

126
00:06:25,291 --> 00:06:27,625
You know, I missed this swing.

127
00:06:27,625 --> 00:06:30,041
When we didn't know
what happened to you,

128
00:06:30,041 --> 00:06:32,458
I'd sometimes imagine you
sitting there.

129
00:06:32,458 --> 00:06:34,708
It's good to see you back.

130
00:06:34,708 --> 00:06:36,166
I'm not back.

131
00:06:36,166 --> 00:06:39,916
I'm not sure I could ever stay
in Master Wu's monastery again,

132
00:06:39,916 --> 00:06:41,666
knowing what he did.

133
00:06:41,666 --> 00:06:44,208
Arin, I know I lied to you.

134
00:06:44,208 --> 00:06:46,333
I let you think
you hit Ras with the--

135
00:06:46,333 --> 00:06:47,541
Sora, please.

136
00:06:47,541 --> 00:06:49,791
I really need to apologize.

137
00:06:49,791 --> 00:06:51,458
No. You don't.

138
00:06:51,458 --> 00:06:54,375
I'm the one
who needs to apologize.

139
00:06:54,375 --> 00:06:57,916
I was so upset
and... embarrassed.

140
00:06:57,916 --> 00:06:59,000
I overreacted,

141
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,583
when you were just trying

142
00:07:00,583 --> 00:07:02,333
to make me feel good
about myself...

143
00:07:02,333 --> 00:07:04,333
like you always do.

144
00:07:06,291 --> 00:07:08,125
Ever since I was a kid,

145
00:07:08,125 --> 00:07:10,375
I had this dream
of being a Ninja,

146
00:07:10,375 --> 00:07:13,750
and then, somehow,
I got my chance, and...

147
00:07:15,875 --> 00:07:19,166
Sora, do you have any idea
how heartbreaking it is

148
00:07:19,166 --> 00:07:22,416
to find out you're not very good
at the thing you love the most?

149
00:07:22,416 --> 00:07:25,375
But you are a good Ninja.

150
00:07:25,375 --> 00:07:27,583
I'm getting better now.

151
00:07:27,583 --> 00:07:30,750
And Ras, of all people,
is helping me do it.

152
00:07:30,750 --> 00:07:33,166
He showed me that I was
holding myself back.

153
00:07:33,166 --> 00:07:35,291
Holding my emotions back.

154
00:07:35,291 --> 00:07:37,375
You've never held back
how you feel, Arin.

155
00:07:37,375 --> 00:07:39,916
You're the sweetest person
I've ever met.

156
00:07:39,916 --> 00:07:42,041
Not those kind of emotions.

157
00:07:42,041 --> 00:07:43,291
My anger.

158
00:07:43,291 --> 00:07:45,791
The hate I feel deep inside.

159
00:07:45,791 --> 00:07:48,000
The stuff I never show.

160
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,666
It gives you a burst of force.

161
00:07:50,666 --> 00:07:52,750
A fuel I've never had before.

162
00:07:57,041 --> 00:07:59,083
[Sora] Look, you know me.

163
00:07:59,083 --> 00:08:00,916
I'm not the best at training.

164
00:08:00,916 --> 00:08:02,083
That's not true.

165
00:08:02,083 --> 00:08:04,750
Last week, I failed
a Spinjitzu exercise so hard,

166
00:08:04,750 --> 00:08:06,583
I got dizzy
and barfed all over Zane.

167
00:08:06,583 --> 00:08:08,666
Okay. Gross.

168
00:08:08,666 --> 00:08:11,916
It's fine, he froze it
so it was easier to clean up.

169
00:08:11,916 --> 00:08:14,458
The point is
I don't know training,

170
00:08:14,458 --> 00:08:16,500
but I do know you.

171
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:20,166
There's no way hate and anger
are your greatest strengths.

172
00:08:20,166 --> 00:08:23,333
The Arin I know,
my best friend,

173
00:08:23,333 --> 00:08:26,041
his strength comes
from his kindness.

174
00:08:26,041 --> 00:08:28,083
His generosity.

175
00:08:28,083 --> 00:08:29,291
His hope.

176
00:08:29,291 --> 00:08:31,208
But all that didn't help me.

177
00:08:31,208 --> 00:08:33,375
It helped me.

178
00:08:33,375 --> 00:08:35,666
And it helped everyone
who ever met you.

179
00:08:39,458 --> 00:08:40,666
[running footsteps] Come on.

180
00:08:40,666 --> 00:08:42,125
They've almost got it.

181
00:08:50,666 --> 00:08:53,375
This was truly
an inspired idea, Lloyd.

182
00:08:53,375 --> 00:08:54,833
Only if it works.

183
00:08:54,833 --> 00:08:56,875
You think that thing
will generate enough power?

184
00:08:56,875 --> 00:08:59,291
Like the time you carried
Source Dragon energy.

185
00:08:59,291 --> 00:09:03,333
Not something I plan on doing
ever again, thank you.

186
00:09:03,333 --> 00:09:05,791
I believe I can increase
the power of our Portal Gate

187
00:09:05,791 --> 00:09:07,916
enough to get
all of us and our gear

188
00:09:07,916 --> 00:09:10,000
through to
the First Land Monastery.

189
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,750
Let's just hope it's in
enough time to cut off Drix.

190
00:09:18,416 --> 00:09:20,833
[powering up]

191
00:09:31,833 --> 00:09:33,666
Whoo-hoo-hoo!

192
00:09:33,666 --> 00:09:35,833
These new gliders
are awesome, Sora!

193
00:09:35,833 --> 00:09:38,750
All thanks to Arin
for getting us a prototype!

194
00:09:38,750 --> 00:09:40,166
Any time!

195
00:09:40,166 --> 00:09:42,458
Alright, let's get back
those blades,

196
00:09:42,458 --> 00:09:44,000
stop the Forbidden Five--

197
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,083
[Kai] And get busy
saving the world!

198
00:09:46,583 --> 00:09:48,708
[all] Ninja, go!

199
00:09:50,250 --> 00:09:52,125
...zero research,
no proper testing,

200
00:09:52,125 --> 00:09:54,416
absolutely no prior experience,

201
00:09:54,416 --> 00:09:57,541
your lack of a medical degree
from an accredited university.

202
00:09:57,541 --> 00:09:59,458
Shall I continue with my list

203
00:09:59,458 --> 00:10:01,875
of why this course of action
is ill-advised?

204
00:10:01,875 --> 00:10:05,583
Ill-advised actions are
my favorite kind of actions.

205
00:10:05,583 --> 00:10:07,875
That fact will now go
on the top of my list.

206
00:10:07,875 --> 00:10:10,291
You got any better ideas,
Dr. Robot?

207
00:10:10,291 --> 00:10:12,583
'Cause if I don't
at least try this,

208
00:10:12,583 --> 00:10:14,833
Roby is definitely gonna die.

209
00:10:16,666 --> 00:10:20,041
There are no courses of action
to my knowledge

210
00:10:20,041 --> 00:10:21,500
that would save Roby.

211
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:22,791
That's what I thought.

212
00:10:22,791 --> 00:10:24,333
Please work.

213
00:10:24,916 --> 00:10:28,208
[crying out]

214
00:10:40,916 --> 00:10:42,791
Blech!

215
00:10:42,791 --> 00:10:44,750
I hate sand on my tongue.

216
00:10:49,625 --> 00:10:51,875
Looks like that's
the center of the winds.

217
00:10:51,875 --> 00:10:54,166
And I'm guessing where
ThunderFang is imprisoned.

218
00:10:54,166 --> 00:10:56,250
If he's still imprisoned.

219
00:10:56,250 --> 00:10:58,416
We'd know if he was free.

220
00:10:58,416 --> 00:10:59,875
[Zane] Then your idea
worked, Lloyd.

221
00:10:59,875 --> 00:11:01,250
Drix has not yet arrived.

222
00:11:05,791 --> 00:11:07,208
How cool is this?

223
00:11:07,208 --> 00:11:09,250
Getting dust
blown in our faces?

224
00:11:09,250 --> 00:11:11,583
I can think of cooler things.

225
00:11:11,583 --> 00:11:14,750
No, being on an adventure
with the Ninja.

226
00:11:14,750 --> 00:11:17,583
Talk about a childhood dream
come true.

227
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,125
[sighing]

228
00:11:21,125 --> 00:11:24,708
I didn't know dreams
could get so complicated.

229
00:11:24,708 --> 00:11:26,166
Blame me, buddy.

230
00:11:26,166 --> 00:11:27,625
For what?

231
00:11:27,625 --> 00:11:30,958
For making you think
Ras's teachings weren't trash.

232
00:11:30,958 --> 00:11:34,875
I'm a stronger Ninja now
than I ever was before.

233
00:11:34,875 --> 00:11:39,625
If you think Ras can teach you
to be a better Ninja than Lloyd,

234
00:11:39,625 --> 00:11:42,791
maybe you don't understand
what a Ninja really is.

235
00:11:46,750 --> 00:11:47,958
[Zane] Everyone...

236
00:11:50,583 --> 00:11:51,500
They're here.

237
00:11:55,166 --> 00:11:56,875
He's waking up!

238
00:11:59,166 --> 00:12:00,750
[Roby] What happened?

239
00:12:00,750 --> 00:12:02,500
I felt like I had a fever.

240
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:05,791
What happened is
you're beautiful again!

241
00:12:07,166 --> 00:12:11,458
I thought that Kur lady
unstanged my zoot for good.

242
00:12:11,458 --> 00:12:13,916
Yeah, well,
I used my vast knowledge

243
00:12:13,916 --> 00:12:16,458
of science and medicine
to cure your decay.

244
00:12:16,458 --> 00:12:17,375
That is not what happ--

245
00:12:17,375 --> 00:12:19,000
Vast knowledge.

246
00:12:20,250 --> 00:12:21,791
So, how we feeling?

247
00:12:21,791 --> 00:12:23,791
Healed, totally fine?

248
00:12:23,791 --> 00:12:25,416
Uh, I think so,

249
00:12:25,416 --> 00:12:27,375
but why,
you got somewhere to be?

250
00:12:27,375 --> 00:12:28,958
The Ninja ran off to fight

251
00:12:28,958 --> 00:12:31,666
some giant dragon
that shoots chaos storms,

252
00:12:31,666 --> 00:12:33,041
and without me--

253
00:12:33,041 --> 00:12:34,500
There's no way
they can survive

254
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:37,041
without their best Ninja.

255
00:12:37,041 --> 00:12:38,250
Go!

256
00:12:38,250 --> 00:12:40,166
I'll be fine.

257
00:12:42,583 --> 00:12:44,958
[♪♪♪]

258
00:12:54,250 --> 00:12:55,291
[revving]

259
00:13:04,875 --> 00:13:07,208
[struggling]

260
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,458
Impossible!

261
00:13:20,583 --> 00:13:23,791
I left you behind
in the World Forest!

262
00:13:23,791 --> 00:13:26,791
You couldn't
have beaten me here!

263
00:13:26,791 --> 00:13:29,083
Ninja are full of surprises!

264
00:13:33,375 --> 00:13:34,458
[roaring]

265
00:13:35,583 --> 00:13:37,041
Attack!

266
00:13:38,333 --> 00:13:40,041
I'll go low, you go--

267
00:13:40,041 --> 00:13:42,333
High! Just like
in the Crossroads!

268
00:14:10,416 --> 00:14:11,291
[snarling]

269
00:14:11,291 --> 00:14:12,250
Whaa!

270
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,500
[Kai] Hey!
Don't hog all the fun!

271
00:14:27,541 --> 00:14:28,750
Did you see that?

272
00:14:28,750 --> 00:14:31,250
My Spinjitzu looked
more awesome than usual!

273
00:14:31,250 --> 00:14:32,416
[Lloyd]
It's a First Land thing.

274
00:14:32,416 --> 00:14:33,791
You get used to it!

275
00:14:36,833 --> 00:14:38,500
[Arin] Whoa, whoa, I need him!

276
00:14:43,375 --> 00:14:44,541
Whew!

277
00:14:49,083 --> 00:14:50,708
Sorry, I'm canceling
the appointment

278
00:14:50,708 --> 00:14:52,500
you and those blades have
with ThunderFang.

279
00:14:53,291 --> 00:14:55,125
[chuckling]

280
00:14:55,125 --> 00:14:59,333
The conqueror's path is rarely
a straight line.

281
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:01,833
[Riyu screeching]

282
00:15:01,833 --> 00:15:03,875
If you did not
understand Riyu,

283
00:15:03,875 --> 00:15:05,375
he said we hypothesized

284
00:15:05,375 --> 00:15:07,666
you would try to escape
via this route.

285
00:15:19,958 --> 00:15:22,208
[Kur] Told you he'd be late.

286
00:15:22,208 --> 00:15:24,916
[Nokt] Late?
I'm betting he failed.

287
00:15:34,958 --> 00:15:37,791
Arin! Free your master!

288
00:15:43,291 --> 00:15:44,541
[Drix crying out]

289
00:15:45,833 --> 00:15:47,125
[Lloyd] Thought
you might do that!

290
00:15:47,125 --> 00:15:49,333
One down, one to go!

291
00:16:02,916 --> 00:16:04,958
[Lloyd] Ninja, we got this!

292
00:16:07,250 --> 00:16:09,833
[laughing]

293
00:16:15,083 --> 00:16:16,416
[gasping]

294
00:16:19,958 --> 00:16:22,083
That belongs to us!

295
00:16:22,083 --> 00:16:23,125
Those things aren't yours

296
00:16:23,125 --> 00:16:25,166
just 'cause
you want them really bad, Rox.

297
00:16:33,625 --> 00:16:36,666
I'm not great at math,
but we are way outnumbered here.

298
00:16:39,416 --> 00:16:42,000
Time for a rematch, girl.

299
00:16:49,916 --> 00:16:52,416
Remind you of that time
I saved you from those bullies?

300
00:16:52,416 --> 00:16:54,541
Uh... why you gotta
bring that up?

301
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,750
Now, who do we have here?

302
00:16:58,750 --> 00:17:01,708
I brought you a present, Nokt.

303
00:17:01,708 --> 00:17:04,166
Priorities, priorities.

304
00:17:07,250 --> 00:17:09,250
I can take him from here.

305
00:17:10,541 --> 00:17:12,416
[grunting]

306
00:17:12,416 --> 00:17:15,083
No! Focus on what matters!

307
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:19,666
Oh, so impulsive,
and so foolish.

308
00:17:19,666 --> 00:17:20,541
Waah!

309
00:17:21,125 --> 00:17:22,166
Ugh!

310
00:17:22,166 --> 00:17:26,125
I've been waiting
a long time for this.

311
00:17:26,125 --> 00:17:27,708
[grunting]

312
00:17:31,416 --> 00:17:35,083
I have no interest
in fighting someone weakened...

313
00:17:35,083 --> 00:17:38,541
like you did to me
with that control collar.

314
00:17:41,875 --> 00:17:44,416
I should never have freed you.

315
00:17:44,416 --> 00:17:46,458
Aw, that hurts.

316
00:17:46,458 --> 00:17:48,208
Because if you didn't free me,

317
00:17:48,208 --> 00:17:51,083
we'd never have moments
like this!

318
00:17:51,750 --> 00:17:52,750
[grunting]

319
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,416
[Drix crying out]

320
00:18:04,083 --> 00:18:04,916
[Arin] Sorry, lady!

321
00:18:04,916 --> 00:18:07,000
You little runt!

322
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,458
Don't you know who
you are messing w--

323
00:18:09,458 --> 00:18:10,416
unh!

324
00:18:24,458 --> 00:18:26,125
I've got it!

325
00:18:32,958 --> 00:18:34,083
[Arin] Riyu!

326
00:18:36,625 --> 00:18:38,333
Arin, we'll hold them off!

327
00:18:38,333 --> 00:18:40,958
Get back to the Monastery
with those!

328
00:18:40,958 --> 00:18:41,958
On it!

329
00:18:49,250 --> 00:18:51,541
Ras... no...

330
00:18:53,208 --> 00:18:55,916
Now, Lord Ras,

331
00:18:55,916 --> 00:18:58,708
let me show you
what real power can--

332
00:19:05,333 --> 00:19:06,208
[grunting]

333
00:19:07,541 --> 00:19:09,416
Arin, no!

334
00:19:09,416 --> 00:19:10,291
Gaah!

335
00:19:12,583 --> 00:19:16,208
Now the little underling
wants to save his master?

336
00:19:16,208 --> 00:19:17,708
Let him go!

337
00:19:17,708 --> 00:19:20,125
I don't take orders from you.

338
00:19:20,125 --> 00:19:22,708
I don't take orders
from anyone.

339
00:19:22,708 --> 00:19:24,500
Then I'll force you to stop.

340
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:27,500
[laughing]

341
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,416
I see you're a comedian.

342
00:19:29,416 --> 00:19:30,750
It's not fun--

343
00:19:35,958 --> 00:19:37,833
[crying out]

344
00:19:37,833 --> 00:19:40,166
[laughing]

345
00:19:40,166 --> 00:19:41,666
Come, my brethren!

346
00:19:41,666 --> 00:19:43,916
It is time!

347
00:19:43,916 --> 00:19:44,791
[Kai crying out]

348
00:19:51,791 --> 00:19:53,750
Come on! We've gotta stop them!

349
00:20:00,958 --> 00:20:03,708
[struggling]

350
00:20:10,083 --> 00:20:11,583
[shrieking]

351
00:20:11,583 --> 00:20:14,708
[struggling]

352
00:20:18,833 --> 00:20:19,708
[grunting]

353
00:20:20,875 --> 00:20:21,875
[grunting]

354
00:20:21,875 --> 00:20:22,875
[screaming]

355
00:20:30,666 --> 00:20:32,250
[crying out]

356
00:20:32,250 --> 00:20:33,333
[impact]

357
00:20:33,333 --> 00:20:35,500
Pixal! Zane! Hold tight!

358
00:20:43,750 --> 00:20:46,083
[pounding]

359
00:20:47,333 --> 00:20:48,541
Aah!

360
00:20:56,708 --> 00:20:57,583
[smashing]

361
00:20:59,708 --> 00:21:00,875
[smashing]

362
00:21:02,625 --> 00:21:04,625
[roaring]

363
00:21:08,041 --> 00:21:10,583
The powers you promised...

364
00:21:11,458 --> 00:21:13,708
My minions,

365
00:21:13,708 --> 00:21:16,125
you are such fools.

366
00:21:16,125 --> 00:21:18,375
If you really trusted me,

367
00:21:18,375 --> 00:21:22,958
you are even more pathetic
than I realized.

368
00:21:24,666 --> 00:21:25,916
[roaring]

369
00:21:27,458 --> 00:21:29,625
[screaming]

370
00:21:40,416 --> 00:21:42,708
[roaring]

371
00:21:45,041 --> 00:21:47,750
[♪♪♪]

